AppleLocalAI includes repository-owned compatibility code derived from Google LLC's
LiteRT-LM Apple Foundation Models adapter and related Swift support in:

  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/CGImagePNG.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTEngineCache.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTErrors.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTLanguageModel.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTLMExecutor.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTSampler.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTSupport.swift
  Backends/Sources/AppleLocalAILocalModels/LiteRTTranscriptPlan.swift

The compatibility implementation descends from Google LLC's LiteRT-LM project
(https://github.com/google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM). The source transfer records commit
091d17598f5107df4e9543eb3b46b4f8d35264bc as the copied-source baseline; this
repository currently resolves the LiteRT-LM runtime dependency at release v0.17.1.
The derived files retain their upstream copyright and Apache-2.0 headers and have
subsequent AppleLocalAI changes for fail-closed transcript/schema handling,
cancellation, resource ownership, and token-usage semantics.

Parts of the upstream Swift implementation acknowledge @john-rocky and
https://github.com/john-rocky/swift-litert-lm/tree/main. Those acknowledgements
are retained in the affected source headers.

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is distributed at:

  LICENSES/Apache-2.0-LiteRT-LM.txt

The LiteRT-LM core runtime and prebuilt artifacts remain external SwiftPM
dependencies and retain their upstream licenses and attribution.
